            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0877" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10/pg845"/>

                <head>352. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="0" xml:id="d352-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-07-14">July 14,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The following is taken from DCI notes used at the meeting on 12 July of the
                    Special Group (Augmented):</p>
                <pb facs="0878" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/>
                <p>We know a lot about Cuba and the following are the essential elements in our
                    assessment of the present situation: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Cuba belongs to Castro.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Castro is apparently strengthening his military forces, and
                            photography and other intelligence have added to our knowledge of the
                            size, composition and deployment of his forces.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Police security appears to be good.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Popular support for Castro has been substantially diminished.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Castro has a number of serious problems including, general economic
                            situation, food, spare parts and lack of competent management of
                            industries and agriculture.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>No splits are apparent in the top leadership.</item>
                        <label>7.</label>
                        <item>We have no penetration at the top.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">WElder</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Executive Assistant/DCI</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
